{"markup": "<div data-component=\"page\" data-slug=\"terms-and-conditions\" data-name=\"page.legal\" data-v-f08e35e9><div data-component=\"legal\" _type=\"page.legal\" name=\"page.legal\" data-v-0d1be5c9><div data-component=\"transition-logo-mask\" data-v-0d1be5c9 data-v-24a16d5c><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\" data-v-24a16d5c><defs data-v-24a16d5c><clipPath id=\"v-0-0-0\" clipPathUnits=\"objectBoundingBox\" data-v-24a16d5c><path d=\"M0.5 0.459184C0.483235 0.501531 0.483824 0.506633 0.476471 0.540816H0.523529C0.516471 0.505612 0.514706 0.496429 0.5 0.459184Z\" data-v-24a16d5c></path></clipPath></defs></svg><div class=\"slot-wrapper\"  data-v-24a16d5c><div data-component=\"header\" _type=\"header\" data-v-0d1be5c9 data-v-31fc84b0><div class=\"header-wrapper\" data-v-31fc84b0><span data-component=\"tag\" data-force-active=\"false\" class=\"span-tag\" data-v-31fc84b0 data-v-a9cd5498><span class=\"label-container\" data-v-a9cd5498><span class=\"-sans-text-3-medium label\" data-v-a9cd5498>Cookies</span></span></span><h1 class=\"header-title xxl-18 xl-18 lg-20 md-22 sm-12 xs-14 -mix-title-3\" data-v-31fc84b0>Delta Cafés Cookie Policy</h1><h2 class=\"header-info\" data-v-31fc84b0><span class=\"-mix-text-2-regular\" data-v-31fc84b0>Updated</span><time class=\"-sans-text-3-medium\" datetime=\"2025-04-04\" data-v-31fc84b0>2025-04-04</time></h2></div></div><main data-v-0d1be5c9><div data-component=\"article-body\" _type=\"body\" data-v-0d1be5c9 data-v-f9679557><div class=\"article-body align-center\" data-v-f9679557><div class=\"article-content\" data-v-f9679557><h2>This Cookie Policy complements the Privacy Policy of Manuel Rui Azinhais Nabeiro, Unipessoal, Lda. (“DELTA CAFÉS”), hosted on the website <a href=\"https://deltacafes.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://deltacafes.com/</a>.</h2><h2>To make your navigation on the website easier, DELTA CAFÉS, NIPC 500 853 975, with registered office at Avenida Calouste Gulbenkian, 7370-025, Campo Maior, informs you that it uses cookies.</h2><h2></h2><h4>What are Cookies?</h4><p>Cookies are files that contain small amounts of information that are downloaded to the user’s device when they visit a website and are intended to enable or improve their browsing experience. Their main purpose is to ensure that the website functions correctly, as well as to recognize the user each time they access the website, while also improving the quality of use and experience, providing better use of the site.</p><h4>Use of Cookies by DELTA CAFÉS</h4><p>Cookies can be classified according to the following categories:<br><br>By origin, cookies can be first-party or third-party, depending on whether the party responsible for sending and originating them is, respectively, DELTA CAFÉS or a third entity.<br><br>By duration, cookies can remain only for the browsing session, in which case they are considered session cookies and are deleted when you close the browser. Alternatively, cookies can remain on your device for longer periods, in which case they are considered permanent cookies.</p><h2></h2><h4>Regarding their function, cookies can be:</h4><p>Strictly necessary, when they are placed to ensure the operation of the Site, to provide features requested by the user, or to store the user’s preferences;<br><br>Personalisation, when they are intended to store and apply preferences on the Site in a simplified and automatic way, in order to improve the user experience;<br><br>Analytics, collecting statistical information about how users use and engage with the Site;<br><br>Advertising, allowing the selection of visible advertising based on the user’s interests.<br><br>Specifically, DELTA CAFÉS is using Cookies for the purposes explained below. If, in the future, DELTA CAFÉS uses other Cookies, the user will be duly informed.</p><h2></h2><h4>Third-party cookies that transfer data to third countries</h4><p>The use of certain third-party cookies on the Site (i.e. personalization, analytics and/or advertising cookies) may involve the transfer of your data to countries outside the European Economic Area (e.g. the United States of America), which may not be subject to an adequacy decision by the European Commission and, as a result, may not offer a level of protection for your data that is essentially equivalent to that of the European Union. For example, the use of Google Analytics cookies may involve the transfer of your personal data (i.e. a unique identifier of your device) to the entities that provide these services and that are established in the United States of America. In these cases, DELTA CAFÉS may not be able to configure how these cookies operate and/or prevent the aforementioned transfer.<br><br>For more information on the data transfers arising from the use of these cookies, please consult our Privacy Policy</p><h2></h2><h4>Your preferences</h4><p>With the exception of strictly necessary cookies, which are placed on your device immediately upon your visit, the implementation of all other cookies depends on your consent. Please note that objecting to the use of cookies may impair your browsing on the Site, and it may not be possible to access some sections and features of our Site, or access may be limited.</p><h2></h2><h4>User setting to avoid cookies</h4><p>If you wish to change your preferences, you can do so at any time here. After adjusting your preferences, you may need to refresh the page so that the new settings are applied.<br><br>You can also change the settings for the use and installation of cookies in your browser (which may affect the operation of our Site, depending on the browser settings panel and the options available to the user). Each browser follows different procedures, so we provide information that allows you to configure your Internet browser or browsers to maintain your privacy and security in relation to cookies. We therefore provide official support information and links for the main browsers so that you can decide whether or not you wish to accept the use of cookies.<br><br>You can block cookies using your browser’s configuration tools, or you can configure your browser to warn you when a server wants to store a cookie:</p><ul><li>Google Chrome</li><li>Microsoft Edge</li><li>Mozilla Firefox</li><li>Microsoft Internet Explorer</li><li>Opera</li><li>Apple Safari</li></ul><p>You can also prevent the processing of your personal data through Google Analytics cookies, on any website, by using the tool available <a href=\"https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</p><h2></h2><h4>Changes to this Policy</h4><p>DELTA CAFÉS may, at any time and without prior notice, change this Cookies Policy. The changes will be duly announced on the Site and, whenever relevant changes are made regarding cookies, you will again see a pop-up notice so that, depending on the type of cookie in question, you can access the information and/or give or withhold your consent to its use and storage.</p><p><br></p></div></div></div></main><footer data-component=\"footer\" data-v-0d1be5c9 data-v-955ea654><div data-component=\"pre-footer\" _type=\"preFooter\" class=\"pre-footer\" data-v-955ea654 data-v-669d83ae><div class=\"background-container\" data-v-669d83ae><img width=\"3400\" height=\"1966\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\" data-nuxt-img onerror=\"this.setAttribute(&#39;data-error&#39;, 1)\" data-component=\"media-asset\" alt=\"Image\" fetchpriority autoplay playsinline=\"true\" muted class=\"media\" data-v-669d83ae data-v-ac455cf8 src=\"/assets/images/7d844bfe2ad433e6df520232098d9147349f3d5a-3400x1966-26a59294f1.jpg\"></div><div class=\"content-container\" data-v-669d83ae><div class=\"upper-title-container\" data-v-669d83ae><div class=\"-mix-label-1 -uppercase upper-title\" data-v-669d83ae>Coffee Science Centre</div><div class=\"-mix-label-1 -uppercase upper-title-overlay\" data-v-669d83ae>Coffee Science Centre</div></div><div class=\"title-container\" data-v-669d83ae><div data-compo